  "implemented": [
    "Actual ProductionUiOwner borrows the protected database and AgentManager, is registered in the real Task API, and retains native snapshot/send flights until raw completion before profile release.",
    "Native main window ownership captures actual raw OS handle, distinct native attachment ticket, document generation and current engine epoch. Trusted completed visible documents alone activate an opaque receipt; navigation, destruction, exhaustion and shutdown fence it. Overlapping page loads conservatively remain unavailable.",
    "Public state payload has no lease or caller grant. Tauri renderer transport captures bootstrap receipt separately; private native ingress checks physical identity/lease and stamps only the sealed engine.ui.publish request. Direct public Source publication and added authority fields refuse.",
    "Each cache read/send refreshes actual native availability and current scalar DB refs; no stale global uiState success. Renderer native intent uses dedicated desktop:ui-command envelope, exact current epoch/receipt and separate lifecycle subscriptions rather than inventing a service event sequence.",
    "Task API checks signed project/task/artifact/parent scopes and current agent/nonce before and after waits. Canvas-derived commands retain their observed document receipt. Accepted transport never claims renderer application; retired/uncertain commands are not replayed.",
    "Finite codecs cap titles, task/panel counts, coordinates, dimensions, Unicode and total UTF8 JSON. SQL scalar bounds precede reference materialization and do not parse unrelated stored credentials/config/descriptions. Commander switch-project awaits actual owned native acceptance.",
    "Actual protected-profile singleton/private pipe and loopback authenticated task API tests prove current publication, wrong/missing token denial, lease retirement and raw acknowledgement drain. Rust complements Source validators and consumes the actual TypeScript corpus."
  ],
